      "sourceTextSha256": "457ad118d1a93f0cae3bcb09d238a8157f55e2df4b0439baec05c50f105fe9a3",
      "text": "Day 2 · Transfer to pick up the motorcycles: at 09:00, handover and briefing about the trip. Then ride to the historic centre to learn about the city’s history and its architectural landmarks, such as the Luz railway station, Praça da Sé and the Cathedral, the Pátio do Colégio where the city was founded, and the Viaduto do Chá. Visit the famous Municipal Market to taste typical Brazilian delicacies and exotic fruits.\n\nAfterwards, explore Liberdade, the heart of the largest Japanese community outside Japan, whose name means “freedom” in Portuguese: an unmistakably East Asian atmosphere, unusual streets, Asian food and shops. Then discover modern São Paulo, with Avenida Paulista, its elegant neighbourhoods and the famous graffiti district.",
